{
  "inShort": "The 28-day goal was missed: neither the playable slice nor five-player testing was demonstrated. Sprint 4 claimed a build and video, but showed a landscape photograph and a film thumbnail. No artifacts were added, so what got done is unknown.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0600jscsz8r4935jty",
      "text": "The public repository remains done. Its demo folders, MIT license and import instructions match the task, but do not demonstrate your game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0s00jtcsz8az0lkwpy",
      "text": "The animated reference video remains accepted as done. The title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny. The video was not watched, so the animated reference remains unverified. Reusing this link in Sprint 4 does not demonstrate the slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1800jucsz8wothj7j8",
      "text": "The playtesting reference article remains done. Wikipedia’s article matches the task, but supplies no evidence of your five-player test."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1q00jvcsz8qpwzz58f",
      "text": "The private design board remains accepted as done without inspection. It does not establish a chosen style from the evidence available."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Did five players complete both islands, the tide loop and co-op sailing?",
    "What failed during those tests, and what did the team learn?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "“Devlog #1” through “Devlog #4” each recorded 0 applause and 0 views; Sprint 4 announced a build without an openable game link, and no store page is listed.",
    "team": "The stated 40–60 hours do not establish delivery pace without playable evidence. Mia stopped confirming after week 1, leaving engineering coverage for co-op sailing unconfirmed while Alex continued confirming work.",
    "management": "Publishing the prototype devlog meets the sole formal stage requirement, but the four closed tasks do not prove the slice or answer the concept’s risks. This evidence gap is common and fixable next checkpoint: publish the two-island co-op build and five-player test notes."
  }
}

